To sort an array of items by their ID and then sum the IDs, you can use the following TypeScript function:

```typescript
interface Item {
  id: number;
}

function sortAndSumIds(items: Item[]): number {
  const sortedItems = items.sort((a, b) => a.id - b.id);
  const sum = sortedItems.reduce((acc, item) => acc + item.id, 0);
  return sum;
}
```

This function first sorts the array of items by their `id` property in ascending order. Then, it uses the `reduce` method to sum up all the `id` values. The sorted array is not returned, but you can modify the function to return it if needed.
